antideepfake-w2v-small.onnx and antideepfake-w2v-small.w0 / .w1 / .w2 are a fine-tuned, converted copy of

    Wav2Vec2-Small-AntiDeepfake
    https://huggingface.co/nii-yamagishilab/wav2vec-small-anti-deepfake
    (revision 9a13264b5dcc827a8d5a4f8e01fccefa392f886b)

by W. Ge, X. Wang et al., Yamagishi Laboratory, National Institute of Informatics (NII), Japan.
Paper: "Post-training for Deepfake Speech Detection", arXiv:2506.21090
Code:  https://github.com/nii-yamagishilab/AntiDeepfake

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

Changes made for VoiceGuard (see ml/train/ and scripts/build_voice_model.py): the transformer
and output layer were fine-tuned on about 20 hours of additional real and synthetic speech
(with simulated phone lines, rooms, noise and codecs), and the result was averaged 50/50 with
the original weights; converted from the original
checkpoint to ONNX; input normalisation built into the graph; parameters used only for
pre-training removed; transformer weights stored as 8-bit integers; weights split across
several files. The converted files are shared under the same licence.

Non-commercial use only. For commercial use, switch to a model whose licence allows it,
for example the bundled AASIST model (MIT): ANTISPOOF_ONNX=ml/models/aasist.onnx
